course: dictionary
lesson: 7874
title: Raisins: dried grapes and dancing snacks
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A raisin is a dried grape: small, wrinkly, brown and sweet. The words around it give you clues. «A box of raisins» and «raisin bread» tell you that raisins are food, something you can eat.
explain: Science gives another clue. «Raisins in lemonade rise when bubbles stick to them like floats and sink again when the bubbles pop at the top.» The raisins are the things that rise and sink. A grape loses water as it dries, and that is how it becomes a raisin.
explain: Context can also warn you about danger. «Some foods that are fine for people are poisonous for pets: onions, garlic, chocolate, grapes and raisins.» So raisins are safe for you, but not for a dog, even when it begs.
fact: A raisin is a dried grape.
fact: Raisins are small, wrinkly, brown and sweet.
fact: In French, «le raisin» means grapes, and a dried raisin is «un raisin sec».
fact: Raisins rise and sink in fizzy lemonade, which makes the «dancing raisins» experiment.
fact: Grapes and raisins are poisonous to dogs, so keep them away from pets.
exercise: What is a raisin? | A small green fruit that grows on trees | A type of fizzy drink | A bread roll with a hard crust | *A dried grape, small, wrinkly, brown and sweet
exercise: «Raisins in lemonade rise when bubbles stick to them like floats.» What makes the raisins rise? | The lemonade gets warm | *Bubbles stick to them | Someone stirs the glass | They are heavier than the lemonade
exercise: Why must you keep raisins away from dogs? | Raisins make dogs grow too big | Dogs cannot chew them properly | *They are poisonous to dogs | Dogs find them too bitter to eat
test: In French, «le raisin» means what? | *Grape | Plum | Raisin bread | Lemonade
test: A grape turns into a raisin when it does what? | Grows bigger | *Loses water and dries | Turns green | Freezes in the fridge
exam: Jayden says, «Raisins are fine for my dog because they are only small.» What should you tell him? | *Raisins are poisonous to dogs, even small ones | Only big raisins are poisonous to dogs | Dogs can eat as many raisins as they like | Small raisins are safe for dogs
